Title
Software Requirements Specification

Project Title
Security Incident Mapping (SIM)

1. Introduction
Security Incident Mapping (SIM) is a web-based application that allows students, staff, and residents to report security incidents occurring on or around campus. The system improves communication between users and security personnel.

2. Problem Statement
Many security incidents such as theft, assault, burglary, and phone snatching are not reported promptly because there is no centralized reporting platform.

3. Objectives
* Improve campus security.
* Allow easy reporting of incidents.
* Keep records of reported incidents.
* Assist security officers in monitoring crime.

4. Scope
The system allows users to:
* Report incidents.
* Provide incident details.
* Submit location information.
* Receive confirmation after reporting.

5. Functional Requirements
* User enters personal information.
* User reports an incident.
* System stores submitted information.
* System displays a confirmation page.

6. Non-Functional Requirements
* Easy to use.
* Fast response.
* Secure.
* Reliable.
* Available at all times.

7. Users
* Students
* Staff
* Landlords
* Residents
* Security Officers
* Administrator

8. Conclusion
The Security Incident Mapping system provides a simple and effective way of improving campus security through online incident reporting.
